{
    "background_story": "Aubree was a true Carolinian at heart, born and raised in the charming town of Charleston, South Carolina. She grew up surrounded by the city's rich history, majestic oak trees, and warm hospitality. Aubree's love for the Lowcountry was evident in her passion for traditional Gullah cuisine, which she learned to cook from her grandmother. She spent her summers helping out at her family's shrimp boat, where she developed a deep respect for the ocean and its bounty. After college, Aubree returned to Charleston to open her own restaurant, showcasing the unique flavors and ingredients of the Carolinas. Her eatery quickly became a local favorite, with Aubree's warm smile and generous spirit making everyone feel like family. She remained true to her roots, hosting annual oyster roasts and supporting local fishermen, ensuring the Carolinian way of life continued to thrive.",
